  "Number": 1,
  "Question": "\\((1+x^2)(1-x^3)\\) equals",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(1-x^5\\)",
    "B": "\\(1-x^6\\)",
    "C": "\\(1+x^2-x^3\\)",
    "D": "\\(1+x^2-x^3-x^5\\)",
    "E": "\\(1+x^2-x^3-x^6\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Multiply each term of the first factor by both terms of the second factor. The product \\(x^2x^3\\) has five factors of \\(x\\), so it equals \\(x^5\\). Thus\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n(1+x^2)(1-x^3)\n&=1-x^3+x^2-x^2x^3\\\\\n&=1+x^2-x^3-x^5.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nThe result is \\(1+x^2-x^3-x^5\\), choice D.",
